                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1][b]STOP BUYING GARBAGE GAMES,\nSTART SUPPORTING WORTHY GAMES LIKE THIS[/b][/h1]\nWhat happened to supporting legitimately good developers?\n\n[b]Pro's[/b]\n[list]\n[*]Sharp and beautiful graphics\n[*]Perfect for family, friends, any inexperienced VR users\n[*]Great game for fans of puzzles, destruction, weapons, furryballs\n[*]Brilliant showcase of VR with hours of replayability\n[/list]\n\n[b]Con's[/b]\n[list]\n[*]No Workshop support (at time of review)\n[*]How has this gone unnoticed? \n[/list]\n\n\nThere are so many games that come out daily it is hard to sift through all the garbage. It is near impossible to find something of quality that is fun, well made and was created by someone that gives a sh☣☣ rather than a company with the deepest pockets and a franchising license. \n[b] A true hidden gem that deserves recognition. [/b]\nSince my purchase of the HTC Vive, I have purchased over 150+ VR titles and played countless more. The main contributing factor to the large VR collection is seeing the limitless capabilities of what these games have to offer, but 95% of those games have less than 1-2hr total play time. That is because the novelty wears off, the actual game inst fun or isn't engaging, after that there's no motivation or reason to invest more time.\n[b]VR Furballs[/b] is something I had honestly passed a few times browsing the store, but I kept noticing it and was unlike any other VR game I had played. The quality of this game far surpasses titles i've seen from large teams and even large companies. The mechanics are well thought out, it feels natural, it looks amazing and tons of replayability. I have spent many hours playing along with my fiance, friends and family. Simple to learn, hard to master. It is the ONLY VR game I have played that is playable and enjoyable in any type of room configuration, standing, sitting, big room, small room or closet. It is also one of the very few that really can be played by anyone, any age and any experience level, even those that get motion sick easily. \n\nIt worries me when near perfect games go unrecognized for no fault of their own, but people are waiting in line to buy another $80 verison of a retextured and renamed version of CoD. This is worth every hard earned dollar, euro, franc, yen, rupee, peso, dong, credit, bells, meso, simoleon or robux  you spend. This is a truly great game and it deserves our support.",
